(2389571, 328058, 36065, '<td valign="top">This shot definitely has some interest to it, but the size is far too small to hold the viewer very long.  I find myself struggling to make out the various elements in the shot.  I think that a much closer vantage point, perhaps from the meadow itself, would have helped a great deal.  While the subject (the goods for sale) is a bit too centered for my liking, the overall composition flows well with the town disappearing over the hill and the goods stretching to the bottom corner of the frame.  The trees at the bottom are also distracting.  Again with the sizing, its really hard to tell if everything is focused or not.  Excellent idea and nice coloring, but definitely some room for improvement.</td>', 'This shot definitely has some interest to it, but the size is far too small to hold the viewer very long.  I find myself struggling to make out the various elements in the shot.  I think that a much closer vantage point, perhaps from the meadow itself, would have helped a great deal.  While the subject (the goods for sale) is a bit too centered for my liking, the overall composition flows well with the town disappearing over the hill and the goods stretching to the bottom corner of the frame.  The trees at the bottom are also distracting.  Again with the sizing, its really hard to tell if everything is focused or not.  Excellent idea and nice coloring, but definitely some room for improvement.', '2006-05-07 10:02:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(2389572, 326474, 47852, '<td valign="top">Ouch!  I find this one strange with the lack of people in the shot.  I would think there would be someone around either looking, helping or cleaning up.  I also can''t figure out how these two vehicles got into this position.  On the positive side though, it definately makes me want to read the article that hopefully accompanies the shot!</td>', 'Ouch!  I find this one strange with the lack of people in the shot.  I would think there would be someone around either looking, helping or cleaning up.  I also can''t figure out how these two vehicles got into this position.  On the positive side though, it definately makes me want to read the article that hopefully accompanies the shot!', '2006-05-07 10:03:00.000000', NULL, 1),
