(2398301, 328113, 19944, '<td valign="top">You just "put this one in" and you still score over a six.  And deservedly so.  Your work is outstanding.  But we all know that.<br/> <br/>But on to more important things...tell us (show us) more about this ballerina on the trampouline......<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-05-09 21:34:48.</i></td>', 'You just "put this one in" and you still score over a six.  And deservedly so.  Your work is outstanding.  But we all know that. But on to more important things...tell us (show us) more about this ballerina on the trampouline......', '2006-05-09 20:51:57.000000', '2006-05-09 22:34:48.000000', 0),
(2398712, 327996, 53572, '<td valign="top">hiya margie, from the ctpii<br/> <br/><b>First Impression:</b> <br/>a classic newspaper shot, with good movement.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>the central element (the three girls) is very good, they are dynamic, and have great interaction.  but the background elements are very distracting, especially the people in the top left.  we start to wonder what they''re doing, and this completey draws out attention away from the action.  the cropping is good, and the girls are in the perfect spots.  well done to get the shot.<br/> <br/><b>Technical:</b> <br/>i think it would pop more with a bit more contrast and saturation.  not a whole lot, it still needs to be a naturalistic, but enough to give rich reds and blacks - they''re a tiny bit faded.<br/> <br/>there''s a tutorial about blurring the background that would come in very handy here.  if the fence and people were blurred, that would bring the focus back to the players, which is where it should be. a little bit of dodgging on the background might help too.  again, not a lot, just enough to draw the eye in to the players.<br/> <br/>i think you could also do a bit more sharpening, just a few strokes of usm, to try to crispit up a bit.<br/> <br/>Summary: <br/>a very good shot, with the potential to be much more.  nicely done.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-05-10 21:35:31.</i></td>', 'hiya margie, from the ctpii First Impression: a classic newspaper shot, with good movement. Composition: the central element (the three girls) is very good, they are dynamic, and have great interaction.  but the background elements are very distracting, especially the people in the top left.  we start to wonder what they''re doing, and this completey draws out attention away from the action.  the cropping is good, and the girls are in the perfect spots.  well done to get the shot. Technical: i think it would pop more with a bit more contrast and saturation.  not a whole lot, it still needs to be a naturalistic, but enough to give rich reds and blacks - they''re a tiny bit faded. there''s a tutorial about blurring the background that would come in very handy here.  if the fence and people were blurred, that would bring the focus back to the players, which is where it should be. a little bit of dodgging on the background might help too.  again, not a lot, just enough to draw the eye in to the players. i think you could also do a bit more sharpening, just a few strokes of usm, to try to crispit up a bit. Summary: a very good shot, with the potential to be much more.  nicely done.', '2006-05-09 23:15:49.000000', '2006-05-10 22:35:31.000000', 0),
(2398776, 326278, 53164, '<td valign="top">hello again.<br/> <br/>while i liked the mystery surrounding the title, i felt the image was a bit too dark.<br/> <br/>the iron gate is nice leading into the hallway, but i did not feel it was the "big story". the bigger story would have been the cache in the prison, not the gate. unless of course the gate is supposed to be the cell. but i did not feel like i was in a cell, but an apartment complex. ifn you had some sort of bed on the other side to signify more of a prison type feel that would have been better. a steel plate and cup. something to make me feel like the darkness is "dark".<br/> <br/>which led me to only looking at the picture for some sort of salvage. i thought the picture stand alone (without title) was like one of my images.... mediocre at best.</td>', 'hello again. while i liked the mystery surrounding the title, i felt the image was a bit too dark. the iron gate is nice leading into the hallway, but i did not feel it was the "big story". the bigger story would have been the cache in the prison, not the gate. unless of course the gate is supposed to be the cell. but i did not feel like i was in a cell, but an apartment complex. ifn you had some sort of bed on the other side to signify more of a prison type feel that would have been better. a steel plate and cup. something to make me feel like the darkness is "dark". which led me to only looking at the picture for some sort of salvage. i thought the picture stand alone (without title) was like one of my images.... mediocre at best.', '2006-05-09 23:35:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(2398796, 328416, 53164, '<td valign="top">hello again,<br/> <br/>i liked this image. thought it was cute.<br/> <br/>what i didnt like was the blown highlights on the guys face. i think had you dropped the exposure a bit... the whole thing would have grown well. the suit could be darker and the fire could be darker. i think that would have got you gallons closer to the ribbon.</td>', 'hello again, i liked this image. thought it was cute. what i didnt like was the blown highlights on the guys face. i think had you dropped the exposure a bit... the whole thing would have grown well. the suit could be darker and the fire could be darker. i think that would have got you gallons closer to the ribbon.', '2006-05-09 23:42:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(2398836, 328213, 53164, '<td valign="top">hello again.<br/> <br/>um<br/> <br/>its like all the same non color. its just white. lol.<br/> <br/>i think what may have been a better idea is to shoot smoke coming from both the car and the smokestack in the background. used a different colored car. that added with the "smokey sky" would have been pretty cool i think. though my images suck pretty badly.<br/> <br/>maybe not so tight a crop on the car too.</td>', 'hello again. um its like all the same non color. its just white. lol. i think what may have been a better idea is to shoot smoke coming from both the car and the smokestack in the background. used a different colored car. that added with the "smokey sky" would have been pretty cool i think. though my images suck pretty badly. maybe not so tight a crop on the car too.', '2006-05-09 23:53:15.000000', NULL, 0),
